"colGroups":[],"rowGroups":[],"cells":[[0,0,1,13,0,1,0,"Class Equipment Restrictions"],[0,13,1,4,1,1,0,"Poison:"],[0,17,1,4,2,2,"R1","?"],[0,21,3,5,3,1,0,"Weapons:"],[0,26,3,16,4,3,"AA1","any"],[1,0,2,4,5,1,0,"Armor:"],[1,4,2,10,6,3,"E2","any"],[1,14,1,3,7,1,0,"Oil:"],[1,17,1,4,8,2,"R2","yes"],[2,14,1,3,9,1,0,"Shield:"],[2,17,1,4,6,2,"R3","any"],[3,0,1,42,10,1,0,"Additional Abilities & Benefits"],[4,0,2,34,11,3,"A5","1. +1 dmg/level against Giant class creatures (bugbears, ettins, giants, gnolls, goblins, hobgoblins, kobolds, ogres, ogre magi, orcs, and trolls).\n"],[4,34,2,4,12,1,0,"Damage Bonus"],[4,38,2,4,13,3,"AM5"],[6,0,4,15,14,3,"A7","4. At 10th level rangers are able to employ all non-written magic items which pertain to clairaudience, clairvoyance, ESP, and telepathy.\n"],[6,15,4,27,15,3,"P7","5. At 10th level, each ranger attracts a body of 2-24 followers. Note that these henchmen once lost, can never be replaced, although mercenaries can be hired, of course. These followers are determined by the DM who then informs the ranger."],[10,0,1,42,16,1,0,"Tracking"],[11,0,1,16,16,1,0,"2. Outdoors"],[11,16,1,26,17,1,0,"3. Underground"],[12,0,3,16,18,3,"A13","Outdoors there is a base 90% chance of a ranger being able to follow a creature, modified as follows."],[12,16,3,26,19,3,"Q13","Underground the ranger must have observed the  creature to be tracked within 3 turns (30 minutes) of the  commencement of tracking, and the ranger must begin  tracking at a place where the creature was observed."],[15,0,2,12,20,1,0,"Circumstance"],[15,12,2,4,21,1,0,"Tracking - Modifier"],[15,16,2,20,22,1,0,"Creature's Action"],[15,36,2,6,23,1,0,"Chance to Track"],[17,0,2,12,24,3,"A18","for each creature above 1 in the party being tracked"],[17,12,2,4,25,2,"M18"],[17,16,1,20,26,2,"Q18","going along normal passage or room"],[17,36,1,6,25,2,"AK18","65%"],[18,16,2,20,26,3,"Q19","passes through normal door or uses stairs"],[18,36,2,6,25,2,"AK19","55%"],[19,0,3,12,24,3,"A20","for every 24 ho